        "ratings": [
            {
                "comment": "Cole's lectures are very good at getting the content across and being a valuable resource for projects and exams. He is also a very nice guy -- willing to meet with you and answer any questions in a way that is not condescending at all like some others in the dept. One of the easier CS electives -- recommend",
                "difficulty_rating": 3,
                "quality_rating": 5
            },
            {
                "comment": "His lectures are detailed. He also gives us a chance to do a project by either one person or in a group, and you can get full scores if you fulfill all requirements. The midterm is very easy and final is fine. Just need to practice past paper and analyze each question, you can get an A",
                "difficulty_rating": 3,
                "quality_rating": 5
            },
            {
                "comment": "Cole Nelson is definitely interested in what he teaches. If you're willing to learn the course material, it shouldn't be too hard. Projects are a bit of work, but not super hard. Cole Nelson definitely wants his students to learn, and I think he does a very good job of this. ",
